{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "3c4d5e6f-7a8b-4c9d-0e1f-2a3b4c5d6e7f",
    "name": "LedgerOne - Inventory (Product)",
    "description": "Inventory module (Product) API collection (Create, Get, Update, List by Company). Reflects the implementation exactly as shipped in apps/api/src/shared/inventory.\n\nDesign note (tenant-owned, X-Tenant-Id always required; header rewrite): identical posture to ProductCategory.postman_collection.json/Unit.postman_collection.json — every /api/v1/inventory/* route sits behind jwt-auth.middleware.ts AND current-tenant.middleware.ts mounted with `{ rewriteHeaderAs: \"decimal\" }` (module-registry.ts), which overwrites `x-tenant-id` in place with the verified JWT claim before this module's own tenantIdHeaderSchema ever inspects it — so a missing/malformed X-Tenant-Id does not itself fail validation here either. No dedicated 'missing/malformed X-Tenant-Id' failure case is included for the same reason.\n\nDesign note (productCategoryUuid is REQUIRED, PCT-001): unlike Unit's optional baseUnitUuid, a Product's productCategoryUuid is required at creation — there is no way to create a valid Product without a real Product Category to reference. This collection therefore includes its own small 'Setup' folder that creates one Product Category (mirroring ProductCategory.postman_collection.json's own Create-Success request pattern) purely as a fixture for the Product folder below, self-contained rather than chaining to the sibling collection.\n\nDesign note (response omits productCategoryUuid/unitUuid, a documented Handbook Deviation, not a bug): product.response.dto.ts deliberately omits both cross-references entirely (an extra Repository lookup per row this milestone's controllers may not make, the same carried-forward reasoning as Unit's/Product Category's own omissions) — not tested for presence or absence beyond the PK-003 internal-field checks.\n\nDesign note (status/isStocked have no transition validation this milestone): create-product.dto.ts/update-product.dto.ts accept `status`/`isStocked` as plain shape-only-validated fields — PRD-003 ('cannot be Discontinued while it has non-zero Stock') and Ch.34.12 ('Stocked classification is fixed once transacted') are both deferred (no Stock/transaction data exists yet to evaluate them against, per create-product.service.ts's own header comment). This collection therefore includes no status-transition-rejection test for Product, a deliberate reflection of that documented gap.\n\nThere is no delete endpoint for Product, so a collection-level pre-request script derives a `{{productSuffix}}` from the current timestamp (once per Newman invocation) appended to every created productCode/name, avoiding cross-run collisions on PRD-001's per-Company productCode uniqueness.\n\nRun order for a full pass, top to bottom: the Setup folder's Product Category and Unit fixtures must run before the Product folder (every Create Product request references {{productCategoryUuid}}/{{unitUuid}}).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
